From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:05:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: nxp-nci: fix NFC dying permanently after a power cycle

Turning the adapter off and on again left NFC dead until reboot. Every
power-on after the first failed with -EREMOTEIO on the i2c read, and the
NCI core then timed out waiting for a CORE_RESET response.

Two things, and only the second is fatal.

The controller needs VEN held low long enough to actually reset.
nxp_nci_i2c_set_mode() waited 10-15 ms in both directions; the vendor
driver waits 100 ms on the way down and 20 ms on the way up. Ten
milliseconds is not enough for a PN553.

The fatal one: a read that fails while the controller is still coming up
latches phy->hard_fault, and nxp_nci_i2c_write() then returns that fault
for every subsequent write. So the NCI reset is never actually
transmitted, and the core sits waiting for a response to a command that
was never sent. hard_fault was only cleared when going to COLD, so a
fault latched during power-up survived every later attempt. A fault
belongs to the power state it happened in -- clear it on every
transition.

Reproduced on a PN553 (Google Pixel 2 XL): before, the second power-on
and every one after it failed. After, four off/on cycles in a row all
succeed.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
index faebc89a7ef5..bbcdd12e8e89 100644
--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
@@ -50,10 +50,32 @@ static int nxp_nci_i2c_set_mode(void *phy_id,
 
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(phy->gpiod_fw, (mode == NXP_NCI_MODE_FW) ? 1 : 0);
 	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(phy->gpiod_en, (mode != NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD) ? 1 : 0);
-	usleep_range(10000, 15000);
 
+	/*
+	 * Powering down needs VEN held low long enough for the controller to
+	 * actually reset. 10 ms is not enough: the part comes back up in a
+	 * state where it NAKs its own address, so the next power-on fails with
+	 * -EREMOTEIO and the NCI reset then times out, leaving NFC dead until
+	 * the machine is rebooted. Reproduced on a PN553 by toggling the
+	 * adapter off and on again.
+	 *
+	 * The vendor driver waits 100 ms here and 20 ms on the way up.
+	 */
 	if (mode == NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD)
-		phy->hard_fault = 0;
+		msleep(100);
+	else
+		usleep_range(10000, 15000);
+
+	/*
+	 * Any bus fault latched before this belongs to the previous power
+	 * state, so clear it on every transition rather than only on the way
+	 * down. A read that fails while the controller is still coming up sets
+	 * hard_fault, and nxp_nci_i2c_write() then refuses every write from
+	 * then on -- so the NCI reset is never actually transmitted and the
+	 * core times out waiting for a response to a command that was never
+	 * sent. That leaves NFC dead until reboot.
+	 */
+	phy->hard_fault = 0;
 
 	return 0;
 }
